;; it-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fencei.s` (P2-SCALAR.4;
;; mirrored to rv64gc-lab-v0 at P4-SYSTEM.2 slice (f), RE-DERIVED at slice (g)).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py it-fencei.expected.sexp schema/expectations.sexp

(comment "it-fencei.expected.sexp — the expected observations for `it-fencei.s`." "" "⛔ EVERY VALUE HERE WAS DERIVED FROM THE PINNED SPECIFICATION PROSE BEFORE THE PROGRAM WAS RUN" "(EVD-05). RE-DERIVATION (P4-SYSTEM.2 slice g, the mirror's fifth): the rv64i original pins the" "cross-model divergence DIFF-FENCEI-EXECUTED — the references nop fence.i because their matched" "configuration excludes Zifencei. That declaration is rv64i's, not this unit's: rv64gc DECLARES" "Zifencei (the ISA string carries it), and the staged encoding leaves the zifencei slot UNBOUND" "((status partial), six slots), so the word decodes RESERVED in the scratch engine today — the" "delivery is this composition's declared refinement, not a profile exclusion. This staging runs" "no cross-model comparison, and rv64gc's references.sexp records no differences, so the" "expect_divergence form is dropped; the semulith-side steps are unchanged and the slot-binding" "leaf re-derives this file to the legal fence.i when the slot binds.")
(expectations (program "it-fencei.s") (entry "0x80000000") (instructions 2) (never_written "x2") (step (n 0) (insn "addi x1, x0, 1") (writes (write (reg "x1") (value "0x0000000000000001"))) (derivation "The ordinary prefix — one write before the fence.i, so the trap's position is observable.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.4")) (step (n 1) (insn ".word 0x0000100F") (writes) (derivation "0x0000100F is fence.i. The staged encoding leaves the zifencei slot unbound, so the word matches no row of the generated decode table: a RESERVED instruction, whose behavior the architecture declares UNSPECIFIED. The laboratory's policy (D-RESERVED-DECODE) converts it to illegal-instruction with tval = the offending word (cause 0x02), and on this composition the trap is DELIVERED (zicsr's declared refinement); the expectations end at the delivered trap, so no handler is observed and x2 — any continuation's marker — is never written.") (source "RVI-RV32I §1.1.5.2 (the reserved-instruction note: UNSPECIFIED) — decision D-RESERVED-DECODE")))
